A||||33||Fierochic88||FieroLisa & FieroChic Go to Williamsburg :)||||10||
Z||000000||Fierochic88||08-06-2001||02:45 PM||||Along with many others that is!  Just got back last night and hope everyone else got home safe and sound!  So far the pics everyone has posted look great though I can't find my car on CoolBlue's page yet!  Guess I gotta keep looking!  <P>What a fun trip!  Our crew (myself, FieroGT 914, BlueLight87, TooManyFieros (my dad) and my mother got in late Thurs. night due to some minor "dipstick" problems on the way down.  A word of caution, be careful when removing your dipstick, cause the whole tube can come with!  Our resident Dipshit (BlueLight87) learned that the hard way!  We met up with FieroLisa & Northstar87 and headed to bed.<P>The next day began with a trip to K-Mart & breakfast with Kenn & Marilyn Anderson.  We then proceeded to get lost around Williamsburg however Chris made a lot of people turn their heads with his Northstar convertible. That afternoon we headed back to the hotel for some rest and some cleaning before heading out to a dinner at the Second Street Bar & Grille that evening with our crew plus OldLar, KSlish, SkiTime & Veronica'sGT, and Mr. & Mrs. Frank Genova.  What a good time we had at dinner complete with making utter idiots out of ourselves by pegging peanuts and other assorted foods at each other (french fry anyone?).  SkiTime is really a good shot!  He hit me right between the eyes!   And I think Old Lar got a good laugh being stuck at the "kid" table :-).<BR>That night more car cleaning ensued as I learned the lighting at the nearby Chevy dealer was perfect to wax my car in!  After some fun time in KSlish's room we all turned it in for the night!<P>Saturday was the show and another good time by all.  That evening after some swimming and relaxing we headed out to the very long banquet (I think FieroPhil had a story for everything).  Chris got 1st in Modified and won Best Engineered and my dad won first in the 85 GT class.  Many other trophies were won by forum members but I'm afraid to list them all cause I know I'll forget someone.<P>What a wonderful weekend had by all, though we all think Ski had the best car in his class and definitely should have won!  We all know his car was one of the neatest and most creative there!  Sunday morning after a nice breakfast at IHop with the crew we headed back home for an uneventful but nice trip.<P>Jennifer<P>------------------<BR>IM Username:  FieroChic88<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/jenscar-sig1.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||skitime||08-06-2001||02:53 PM||||Thanks Jen for your thoughts on my car.  I guess I just have to work on it more.  I was worried I would have to be hauling your car home on the trailer but ended up hauling Jasons after his rear brake line broke.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroLisa||08-06-2001||04:19 PM||||My thoughts on the show:<P>Skitime: Your car is friggin AWESOME. I'm amazed at the things you have done to it.<P>Jen(Fierochic88): Fun time, we have to get together before Daytona... Ohio, say Columbus, is right in the middle of all of us  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Chris(Northstar87): OK, nothing exciting, as usual you brought home triple the amount of trophies I did.<P>LZeitgeist and Formula88: Pat, nice to see you again, John, good to meet you, hopefully see you at the get together at the end of August.<P>KSlish: I'm just jealous that I didn't get to sleep in your bed. I mean, I am your fiancee and everything.<P>109 Fieros showed up total! <P>I will have over 80 pics of the show up on my website sometime this week. Right now I have like 3 pics, but all are of my car, and that's not so fun for the rest of you, but here is the link: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/williamsburg.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierolisa/williamsburg.html</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
Z||000003||LZeitgeist||08-06-2001||05:14 PM||||Lisa - it was great seeing you again, too... I *love* the 'Violent Grape'  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> - it's even purtier than the pics show.<P>I hate that it didn't win anything this time around, but I gotta say that I'm glad I wasn't in the same classification as you! Man, that competition was BRUTAL!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||kslish||08-06-2001||06:08 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>Chris(Northstar87): OK, nothing exciting, as usual you brought home triple the amount of trophies I did.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hell, Chris was still recieving trophies from LAST year's show!!!<P>And Lisa, yea you probably won't let me live down the bed thing, but remember...I did hook you up with a certain "something" Friday afternoon while you were cleaning your car, don't you forget that!! <P>After all, I don't want to ruin our plans for Vegas in a couple years   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ken<P><p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 08-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wild_86_Custom||08-06-2001||06:19 PM||||Hello everyone this is my first time posting a message. I was told while in Williamsburg that I needed to get on the Forum and be active.<P>Oh ya so everyone knows who I am I am Kurtis I have a 86 Fiero SE (mild custom) and a 86 Fiero GT (wild custom) <P>I took the GT to Williamsburg and had a great time I got to meet a lot of new people and I really enjoyed the cars.||||reg||1
