Z||000012||Veronica's V6 GT||08-06-2001||11:24 PM||||Hi Girls, you both did a fantastic job of preparing your cars, they looked great!  I had a lot of fun with the both of you at banquet and the 2nd Street Tavern. Jen, just one more strawberry daiquai and you wouldn't have felt that peanut when it hit the middle of your forehead, good shot skitime.  Lisa, I hope you were able to find all peanuts that flew your way, if you know what I mean. Thanks also to Jim and Cindy, Jason and Rebecca, Chris, Joe, Matt and Ken for the good times. We will be on vacation for next 3 weeks, it will be a blessing not to have to clean my car for a while all though I did feel the need to wash my car before we went on vacation. Couldn't leave her for three weeks dirty.  I'll see you around at the fall shows. Again great job both of you and I'll see ya soon.<P>Vonnie||||reg||1
Z||000013||Old Lar||08-07-2001||12:36 PM||||Old Lar had fun at the Kids table considering I was twice the age of the oldest kid.  It was "interesting" to see things haven't changed much as far as clevage peanut dunking or ice dunking (more reaction with ice).  <BR>Modified or custom class cars was real hard at this show.  Lots of real nice cars with nice displays.  The Session boys really know how to put nice cars together and then to have Old Lar's 88 GT parked next to one at the show.  No comparison on good looks for a car. <BR>Twin Lakes did a good job putting my car together cause it ran flawlessly, getting over 30 mpg even when I was stuck in an I-95 traffic jam on idle for an hour.  No overheating at all.  I began to think the temp guage was broken cause it never moved.   I shut off the A/C and it did go up a little.  Turned back on and it went back down. The delay made for a long drive home.  I got to clean off the bugs last night.<P>I'll stick some of the digital photos that came out on the forum somewhere. I got them into a folder on my computer, now it is time to review them to see how they look on the monitor. I took nearly 200 when I include the traditional silver halide film.<BR>I'll only post the nice ones of Lisa and Jennifer.||||reg||1
